Delta_{aa,baa} = x**2 - x*z + y - 2   (lengths 2,3)
Delta_{AB,ABB} = x - y*z + z   (lengths 2,3)
PASS  Delta_{aa,baa} == h exactly (coefficient 1, not (y+1) or (y^2+y-1))
PASS  Delta_{AB,ABB} == -q exactly
PASS  Delta_{aa,baa} in P0  (=> Phi(tau_aa)=Phi(tau_baa), a legitimate J_3 generator)
PASS  Delta_{AB,ABB} in P0  (=> Phi(tau_AB)=Phi(tau_ABB), a legitimate J_3 generator)
PASS  <Delta_{aa,baa}, Delta_{AB,ABB}> == <h,q> == K  (Groebner bases coincide)

CONCLUSION: K = P0 cap I(N) = <h,q> is generated by two trace
            differences of words of length <= 3 (aa/baa, AB/ABB),
            both independently confirmed to satisfy the defining
            collision condition. Combined with the already-proved
            J_L subseteq K for every L (Theorem 5.7's upper bound,
            unconditional in L) and K subseteq J_3 (from these two
            witnesses), the chain K subseteq J_3 subseteq J_infty
            subseteq K closes, giving

            J_infty = J_3 = J_4 = J_5 = P0 cap I(N) = <h,q>.

            This STRENGTHENS Theorem 5.7 as published (which states
            J_infty=J_5): the same ideal is already generated by
            collisions of word length <= 3, not merely <= 5. The
            statement J_infty=J_5 remains true; J_infty=J_3 is a
            strictly stronger, equally exact fact.
